News - Why Printed Circuit Board Prices Go up in 2021?Why Printed Circuit Board Prices Go up in 2021?
Since the mid of 2020, the whole electronics and electrical industry has been witnessing the printed circuit board prices climb higher and higher, and this leads to higher prices of the end-products. Why printed circuit board prices rise in 2021?
Materials for PCB Production Rocket In the printed circuit board supply network, there are three parts – raw materials, copper-clad laminates, and PCB manufacturing.
Since the costs of the raw materials and CCLs soar, the downstream PCB industry struggles.
Now you may realize the main reason for the increase in PCB prices is the higher and higher copper price.
Besides, other main PCB materials’ prices also go up significantly, such as the glass fiber. For example, one of the world’s largest CCL companies, claimed another price increase of glass fiber on November 30th,2020.
This is because the profit rate of making standard PCB copper foils are much lower than making lithium copper foils used for new energy vehicles. As new energy vehicles are in growing demand, the copper foil manufacturers assign more production in lithium copper foils, and there leave fewer production lines for the standard PCB copper foils.
