High-frequency PCB is an antenna PCB that generates, evaluates, emits, and receives radio-frequency signals of more than 1GHz.
The most basic high-frequency PCB has 4 layers and consists of the RF system and the digital circuit.
All PCB wires are supposed to transfer the signals rather than emit them. While one PCB antenna emits them, and the other receives the reflected signals.
All the above functions of the high-frequency PCB are achieved thanks to the PCB’s base materials. The high-frequency materials transmit high-frequency signals to antennas with the smallest possible attenuation.
Low water absorption. Moisture elevates Dk and Df, so the materials should have low water absorption.
Good chemical and impact resistance and peel strength. High-frequency PCBs are usually used in aggressive environments, so they should have these features.
