Let’s first talk about a few concepts:
The video surveillance system is mainly composed of four parts: front-end camera part, transmission part, control part, display and recording. The system enables managers to observe and record the activities of all personnel in the front-end guard area in the control room, and provide dynamic image information for the security system.
The architecture of the two systems is basically composed of audio and video acquisition equipment and server-like equipment. For video conferencing, it is composed of conference terminals and MCU (multipoint control unit); for video surveillance, it is composed of cameras and hard disk recorders (or PC servers), which are basically star-shaped structures centered on server-like equipment .
