If you are new to the game, you probably don't know how to get food in Rust, so this guide is perfect for you, as we will tell you the best places to find these important resources before you start working.
La rule number 1 to survive in Rust is for the player to make sure they have enough food and water to survive.
Clean drinking water is fairly easy to come by, as players can drink from any body of water on the map, other than the ocean, to replenish the character's hydration.
Each server has NPCs that will sell food, but that requires players to have at least some leftovers to trade.
Rivers can be easily seen on the map as they are long, thin bodies of water that generally connect to the ocean. These places are great for the new players visit them first as you can safely fill your hydration meter by drinking from the river, and there is plenty of food nearby.
This makes rivers one of the best places to set up camp, as players will not have to worry much about the basic necessities of Rust.
