Many users of the Apple brand constantly wonder why Pou it is paid on iPhone and all iOS devices. Well, it's time we answer the question.
So, if you are asking yourself this same question, make yourself comfortable and read on, because you will finally know the answer.
If you have come to compare the Google Play Store with the App store, surely you have realized that more than one application is totally free (some only in the first instance, but we will touch on this point later) on Android while that same application , exactly the same in everything, but on iOS, it asks you to please touch your pockets to download it.
The reasons we find have more weight to know why Pou is paid on iPhone, they are the following:
This means that there are tens (if not hundreds) of millions more Android devices than iOS. And that brings us to the next point.
As you should know, in Pou can get some coins watching advertising. That publicity is gambling money.
Android has (in this assumption, because we know that there are many more) one million more users than iOS, which translates into more advertising for Google's operating system, and more revenue for the game from this platform.
So that, to stay in the App Store and to be able to make a profit, because iPhone users are much less than Android users, they must charge to install the game and thus get enough money for everyone.
Bull's story from Brawl Stars It is, like that of almost all the characters in the game, a total mystery, however, Supercell has given some clues as to what its true origin could be, and it is something that this time we have decided to bring it for you.
This Brawler Common He is one of the characters that attracts the most attention thanks to his appearance of ruthless Elvis and that big bull ring that hangs from his nose. Bull belongs to the Heavy Weight.
His main attack is to empty his shotgun by unleashing a burst of shots that can be deadly the closer he is to the enemy.
As we told you at the beginning, the history of Bull, and its origin, is a mystery, but the clues that Supercell has thrown are enough for us to build a story.
During his teenage years, he decided to join his school's football team as he had excellent tank skills.
He was a living legend among the students. But Bull was not only famous for his talent on the field, he was also famous for his bad attitude towards his teammates, whom he attacked on several occasions.
With a contained rage over what happened, Bull decided to go against his coach, who sent him to the hospital with multiple fractures.
On the way he met Crow, with whom he would start a band that he would later join Bibi, as her lover and her accomplice.
Unfortunately, they were unable to secure the security of the institution and the three were arrested, but being too dangerous even for the inmates, it was decided to send them to Brawl Stars To serve his sentence by fighting forever.
We hope you liked Bull's story in Brawl Stars. If so, don't forget to leave us your opinion in the comment box.
