It is normal to wonder what subs are on Twitch, as there is a big difference between "followers" and "subscribers" on this successful streaming platform.
That is why this time we decided to bring you not only the differences between one and the other, but also the benefits they bring.
Subscriptions Twitch They are a class of "patrons" who make a monthly payment as a way of supporting our favorite channels within the platform.
Subscriptions are one of the most popular ways to earn money on Twitch.
Subscribing and following on Twitch is not the same.
Subscribing, on the other hand, is a way to financially support a Twitch channel by opting for regular monthly donations.
While most viewers subscribe to the channels primarily to support their favorite streamer, there are also several tangible benefits to opting for the recurring monthly payment.
Exclusive chat room- Twitch partners and affiliates have the option to create a dedicated chat room for their broadcasts that can only be accessed by paying subscribers. This can be useful for popular channels that have thousands of followers commenting all at once in the chat, which can essentially render it useless.
Ad-free display- Many streamers choose to reward their subscribers with an ad-free viewing experience. This removes all pre, mid, and post-roll video ads from your stream.
To subscribe to a Twitch channel, you must visit the website official on a computer, or from the browser of your mobile device, log in and follow the following steps:
Select Subscribe | $ 4.99 to choose the default monthly subscription fee of $ 4.99 USD. Or choose All Paid Levels to choose the $ 9,99 or $ 24,99 payment option and see a list of benefits for each subscription level.
The Twitch subscription will begin as soon as your chosen payment method is processed. Related Posts
