This great game was developed and released by Supercell, same company of Clash of Clans, so it doesn't surprise you if you find out that both games are aptly named cousins.
That is why it is considered normal that many of the players constantly ask themselves: What does it mean Clash Royale in Spanish?
Clash = Clash, Showdown.
Therefore, playing both words we can obtain the phrase Real crash o Royal clash. However, many times the translations that you can find on the internet can be inaccurate or tend to sound ugly to how it could sound in Spanish, so the most correct translation would be: Royal Showdown.
This allusion to the essential of the game, since, after all, Clash Royale it is about winning battles against other kings and their knights.
